      "content": "thanks for the summary. i noticed u flagged the \"colloquial expressions\" as something that requires \"additional review.\" \n\nto help with my report, i'm trying to figure out if there's a trend here. when you see these kinds of patterns—like the \"ain't\" or the dropping of certain consonants—is it usually just random informality, or is it typically a sign of a specific dialect or demographic? basically, is there a way to predict which callers will be \"high complexity\" based on how they sound?",
